                "metadata": {
                    "category": "music",
                    "author": "The Kanneh-Masons",
                    "description": "The Kanneh-Masons are a family of seven talented siblings who love playing music together. ‘River of Music’ celebrates the sources of their musical inspirations: home, love and family. It includes classical favourites, folk songs, and spirituals. \n\nFrom Schubert’s charming ‘Trout Quintet’ which the siblings spent their childhood listening to, Samuel Coleridge-Taylor’s “Deep River” to traditional Welsh hymns like “Ar Lan y Môr”, the music honours the family’s roots and the stories passed down through generations. The perfect introduction to classical music.    \n\n“This is a story about our family and the sources of our music. Music runs like a river through the generations, and our passion for listening and playing music comes from our grandparents, and from their stories, flowing from the places and dreams they passed on” – The Kanneh-Mason Family",
                    "audioPreviewUrl": "https://audio-previews-media.api.yotoplay.com/audio-previews/c2ac1595563a9857899a22457c1b13c0c963f359d4e88e8fb99f3d76def24d80/JmJ6NMHRJwJuj50xTbuRLrW1i3pBXkqjZpXYTBuZ_z8.mp3",
